  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "If you experience sudden abdominal pain after meals, it is important to seek medical attention immediately. Some warning signs to watch for include:\n\n  1. Severe pain that is sharp, stabbing, or burning\n  2. Pain that is accompanied by nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea\n  3. Pain that is localized to one area of the abdomen\n  4. Pain that is accompanied by fever, chills, or jaundice\n  5. Pain that is persistent or worsening over time\n\nIf you experience any of these warning signs, it is important to seek medical attention immediately. Your doctor will be able to determine the cause of your abdominal pain and recommend appropriate treatment.",
